  "limits": [
    "The original v8 native driver completed prune/restart/backup/shutdown, then failed because the generic privacy observer expected an unused application-secret field. Read-only finalization checks known credential values and absence of every full builder-token format, and independent audit verifies actual state/snapshot. The failed driver stays unaccepted; native effects are not replayed.",
    "V7 remains closed because its immutable image lacks the retention correction. V8 is also a closed candidate; full admission and received/versioned installation of this exact successor remain separate gates.",
    "Native v8 covers pruning, HTTP/D1 data, restart and a stopped snapshot; a fresh v8 restore of the combined pruning/history metadata is not claimed here.",
    "V7 background and diagnostics audits remain bounded evidence for the recorded v7 image. The inheritance map is read-only reuse evidence, not fresh native failure or performance testing.",
    "The first isolated full-suite run failed because macOS canonicalizes /tmp to /private/tmp and existing stack-privacy tests reject the word private. It remains unaccepted. The final suite runs from the normal checkout with assertions unchanged.",
    "The initial v8 packaging attempt stopped before building because source inventory encountered dependency symlinks in the isolated checkout. The successful attempt supplies a process-local Git exclusion for those dependency links. No failed attempt is reported as passing.",
    "The initial background and inheritance audit readers used incorrect receipt-field names. Their failures are retained; corrected independent audits verify the actual stored fields without repeating native effects.",
    "Guide/status text is edited after the executed source archives. The listed executable and test inputs match the native v8 archive.",
    "No existing user installations or user-installation migrations. QA stacks and their data remain retained. Global Docker context stays unchanged.",
    "Private cached-parent COPY-only packaging; no native rebuild, dependency install, registry publication, download publication or official versioned release.",
    "No per-worker CPU quota, broad density, separate physical machine, power-loss or exactly-once external-effect claim. No external review approval is inferred."
  ]
}
